THOUGHT: NullAway complains because Stream is nullable and dereferenced in ShiftLow without a check. Other methods (FlushStream) already guard Stream with a null check, and ReleaseStream can set it to null. To fix only this error without changing behavior, I’ll add a local null check around the write loop in ShiftLow. Then I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '64,76s/^/@@@/;/@@@  public void ShiftLow()/,/@@@	  }\$/{
s/@@@//;
}' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/compression/rangecoder/Encoder.java && sed -i '64,76c\  public void ShiftLow() throws IOException {
    int LowHi = (int) (Low >>> 32);
    if (LowHi != 0 || Low < 0xFF000000L) {
      _position += _cacheSize;
      int temp = _cache;
      if (Stream != null) {
        do {
          Stream.write(temp + LowHi);
          temp = 0xFF;
        } while (--_cacheSize != 0);
      } else {
        _cacheSize = 0;
      }
      _cache = (((int) Low) >>> 24);
    }
    _cacheSize++;
    Low = (Low & 0xFFFFFF) << 8;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/compression/rangecoder/Encoder.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .*errors" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

